    historyContent: {
      origins: "Part of the modern 'Mixed Game' evolution in high-stakes poker rooms. It was popularized by players who enjoyed the complexity of Deuce-to-Seven Lowball and wanted to add a Badugi component back when Badugi was the newest trend in the mid-2000s.",
      originCountries: [
        'United States',
      ],
      timeline: [
        "Mid-2000s: Emerges in California 'Big Game' mixes.",
        "2010s: Becomes a standard rotation in WSOP 'Dealer's Choice' and 'Mixed Triple Draw' events.",
        'Present: Highly regarded as one of the most strategically deep draw games in professional poker.',
      ],
      evolution: "Badeucy is considered more 'pure' than Badacey by many experts because the Ace-high constraint makes hand-building significantly more difficultâ€”you cannot use the Ace for your Lowball half.",
      cultural: "Regarded as a game where 'every card counts', demanding extreme discipline in starting hand selection.",
